 "segments": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "s": 0.35,
   "e": 3.874,
   "text": "So far, this has been a story of failure.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.524,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "s": 4.094,
   "e": 5.367,
   "text": "But there is a twist.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.273,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "s": 5.984,
   "e": 8.32,
   "text": "And it changes everything.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.336,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "s": 9.265,
   "e": 11.785,
   "text": "Go back to the Hebbian memory from chapter four:",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.52,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "s": 11.93,
   "e": 20.102,
   "text": "the matrix that stores associations by adding up outer products, value times key-transpose. We watched it drown in crosstalk.",
   "dur": 8.172,
   "voiced": 491,
   "sim": 0.866,
   "f0": 120.962,
   "st": 0.138,
   "range_st": 6.631,
   "asr": 0.81,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "s": 21.25,
   "e": 23.22,
   "text": "Now look closely at a Transformer.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.97,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "s": 23.44,
   "e": 25.76,
   "text": "Strip the softmax out of attention,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.32,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "s": 26.09,
   "e": 29.185,
   "text": "and something extraordinary is left behind.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.095,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "s": 30.284,
   "e": 35.609,
   "text": "Every new token writes its value, times its key-transpose, into a running matrix.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 5.326,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "s": 35.829,
   "e": 39.077,
   "text": "Every query reads from that matrix, by multiplication.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.248,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "s": 40.131,
   "e": 41.846,
   "text": "That is Hebb's rule.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.715,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "s": 42.197,
   "e": 42.731,
   "text": "Exactly.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 0.534,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "s": 43.431,
   "e": 49.061,
   "text": "In 2021, Imanol Schlag, Kazuki Irie and J\u00fcrgen Schmidhuber proved it formally.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 5.631,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "s": 49.541,
   "e": 60.38,
   "text": "Linear attention is a fast weight programmer: a slow network that learns, by gradient descent, to write fast synaptic weights while it is thinking.",
   "dur": 10.838,
   "voiced": 624,
   "sim": 0.728,
   "f0": 117.853,
   "st": -0.313,
   "range_st": 7.17,
   "asr": 0.917,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "s": 61.08,
   "e": 64.595,
   "text": "The idea is older than the Transformer itself.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.516,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "s": 65.081,
   "e": 73.112,
   "text": "In 2016, Jimmy Ba and Geoffrey Hinton argued that brains have synapses that change faster than learning, but slower than thought,",
   "dur": 8.03,
   "voiced": 522,
   "sim": 0.871,
   "f0": 121.992,
   "st": 0.285,
   "range_st": 6.116,
   "asr": 0.87,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "s": 73.732,
   "e": 77.91,
   "text": "and that these fast weights are a neurally plausible way to attend to the recent past.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.178,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "s": 79.122,
   "e": 82.389,
   "text": "So the Transformer never rejected Hebb.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.267,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "s": 83.196,
   "e": 85.59,
   "text": "It moved Hebb out of the synapse...",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.394,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "s": 86.21,
   "e": 87.939,
   "text": "and into the activations.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.729,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "s": 88.85,
   "e": 89.845,
   "text": "And the crosstalk?",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 0.995,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "s": 91.095,
   "e": 95.387,
   "text": "Schlag's team showed that pure outer-product writing hits a hard capacity wall.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.292,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "s": 95.96,
   "e": 97.48,
   "text": "Their fix was the delta rule:",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.52,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "s": 97.57,
   "e": 101.914,
   "text": "before writing, read what the memory already predicts, and store only the error.",
   "dur": 4.344,
   "voiced": 288,
   "sim": 0.802,
   "f0": 116.024,
   "st": -0.583,
   "range_st": 6.964,
   "asr": 0.769,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "s": 102.835,
   "e": 104.974,
   "text": "We tested this on this laptop.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.139,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "s": 105.194,
   "e": 108.733,
   "text": "With thirty-two associations in a sixty-four dimensional memory,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.539,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "s": 108.926,
   "e": 112.313,
   "text": "pure Hebbian writing recalled only forty-nine percent of them.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.387,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "s": 112.779,
   "e": 116.366,
   "text": "The delta rule recalled seventy-eight percent in a single pass,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.587,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "s": 116.542,
   "e": 118.982,
   "text": "and every single one after three.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.44,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "s": 119.788,
   "e": 122.136,
   "text": "This is exactly where the frontier is moving.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.348,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "s": 122.593,
   "e": 126.256,
   "text": "DeltaNet and Gated DeltaNet add a forgetting gate to the delta rule.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.663,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 31,
   "s": 126.846,
   "e": 132.525,
   "text": "Google's Titans go further still: a neural memory that rewrites its own weights at test time,",
   "dur": 5.679,
   "voiced": 359,
   "sim": 0.833,
   "f0": 118.857,
   "st": -0.166,
   "range_st": 4.848,
   "asr": 0.788,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 32,
   "s": 132.618,
   "e": 136.857,
   "text": "driven by surprise, the gradient of how wrong it just was.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.239,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 33,
   "s": 137.972,
   "e": 140.452,
   "text": "Self-adapting intelligence did arrive.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.48,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
